-- ...and the fourth sweep, which the third layer created the moment it was
-- declared. Its residue is the largest of the four because most kinds transfer
-- no control at all — an identifier, a literal, a property — and that is
-- arithmetic rather than judgement, which is exactly what a sweep is for.
-- DONE 2026-09-05, and the number is the argument against calling a sweep
-- arithmetic: FORTY cells, TWENTY-EIGHT genuine residue, TWELVE not. A default
-- would have said `not_yet` about all forty and been wrong about twenty-eight;
-- a blanket waiver would have been wrong about twelve. The twelve fall into
-- four questions and each got an item of its own rather than a bucket.
work(w_cf_sweep, "DONE 2026-09-05: 40 cells, 28 waived with a reason, 12 that were not residue split into four items").
