-- 54 - meta_property.
work(w_meta_property, "new.target and import.meta: one node kind and two questions").
-- PARTLY DONE 2026-09-08, and the item stays OPEN with three of its four cells
-- unanswered ON PURPOSE. Closing them would need one verdict to cover two
-- constructs, and the measurement says they are two.
--
-- THE SCANNER DISTINGUISHES THEM AND NOTHING ABOVE IT DID. Measured: a
-- `meta_property` node carries ZERO `ast_attr` rows of any key and exactly two
-- identifier children, `meta` and `property` — so `new.target` is
-- (meta="new", property="target") and `import.meta` is
-- (meta="import", property="meta"). The distinction was on the store the whole
-- time and no relation read it, which is the shape this loop keeps finding.
--
-- WHAT WAS ANSWERED, AND IT IS NOT ONE OF THE FOUR LAYERS. The ERA table said
-- `kind_needs(js, meta_property, meta_property)` with `feature_since(...,
-- 2015)`, and that is WRONG FOR HALF THE KIND: `new.target` is ES2015 and
-- `import.meta` is ES2020. Neither refinement the era layer already had could
-- split it — `attr_needs` reads an attribute and there is none, and
-- `outside_attr_needs` reads an ANCESTOR while the difference is inside — so a
-- FOURTH gate table, `child_needs(Lang, Kind, Field, Name, Feature)`, was
-- written beside them. `uses_kind[audit](meta_property, F)` now returns two
-- features five years apart from one node kind, and es2015 refuses exactly the
-- later one.
--
-- ONE CELL CLOSED. `controlflow` is waived, and the reason is measured rather
-- than borrowed from the neighbours: a `meta_property` contains exactly its two
-- identifiers and neither is a `site[code]`, with a positive control that the
-- containment query does return sites for a node that has one. Both forms are
-- LEAVES — two tokens joined by a dot, and neither token is a lookup.
-- DONE 2026-09-08. All four cells answered, and the three that were open closed
-- on ONE measurement rather than on four rules: the reason all three carried is
-- false, because `axis_applies(shape, modules)` was already declared and the
-- column is per-layer by design. See the three notes below.
work_state(w_meta_property, done).
-- ...AND THE DEPENDENCY IS WITHDRAWN, measured. It read: the item waits on the
-- standard library by name for half of one cell, because `unresolved_call` on
-- `import.meta.resolve` would sit in `w_env_api_surface`'s in-tray. It cannot:
