--
-- callgraph, SPLIT AND BOTH HALVES ANSWERED. `new.target` in callee position is
--   the constructor of the CURRENT INVOCATION — measured on V8 13.6, `Derived`
--   and not `Base` inside `Base`'s constructor under `new Derived()`, and
--   `undefined` in a plain call — so `runtime_dependent`, irreducible.
--   `import.meta` is NEVER a callee (`import.meta()` is a TypeError), so it is
--   waived; its only call-graph position is as a RECEIVER, and that call is
--   `member_expression x s_member_on_meta`, which now has a site
--   (`import.meta.resolve(spec)` in shapes.ts) and its own irreducible verdict.
--   THE NOTE'S OWN OBJECTION IS DISCHARGED RATHER THAN IGNORED: it kept the site
--   out because it would land in `s_member_on_other` and falsify that shape's
